  "notes": "Cash basis county, FY ended 2024-06-30. No business-type funds. Governmental figures from the Total Governmental Funds column (pp5-6). Taxes 5,913,916 split by the Statement of Activities general receipts (p2): Property 5,534,757 + Motor vehicle 372,898 + Lodging 6,261 = 5,913,916 (Inheritance 687,547 is its own statement line). Local 1,502,351 kept as one line (broad group; no category over half per p2). Debt service 'Principal and interest' 515,225 (p6) split into principal 500,000 and interest 15,225 using the Road Impr Bond Fund column of the nonmajor combining statement (p9). Sale of assets 29,727 -> other_financing. Reclassification of funds (Note 13) moves 861,933 from nonmajor funds to the Highway Buyback Fund and nets to 0 in the total column. Roll-forward 9,966,959 + 10,909,815 - 11,965,021 + 29,727 + 2,723,282 - 2,723,282 = 8,941,480. Detail: General Fund from its budget schedule (p10, departments not itemized; its Local includes sale of assets 29,637); Inheritance Tax Fund and Veteran's Aid Fund columns from the General Fund combining statement (p7); Road, American Rescue Plan and Highway Buyback budget schedules (pp11-13; Highway Buyback budgeted disbursements 1,106,003 with actual 0 not recorded); the non-major combining statement has 14 fund columns, so its Total Non-Major Funds column is used (p9). General Fund taxes stay unlabeled in detail: other funds' taxes (Health Department 129,961, Road Impr Bond 431,740) are not proven to be a single type, so subtraction is not used. Balance sheet: governmental funds Statement of Assets and Fund Balances (pp3-4, Total column), whose totals equal the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1). Read pages 1-13 of 13"
}
